        "original_id": "839104dd-fef2-5daf-9be1-292cb8786366",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jimmy Hoffa, Danny DeVito, David Mamet, Jack Nicholson, John Joseph Nicholson, Robert Ciaro, Karen Black, Susan Anspach, Ralph Waite, Sally Struthers, László Kovács\n- Films: Hoffa, Five Easy Pieces, Easy Rider\n- Organizations: Teamsters\n- Roles: actor, filmmaker, director, writer, cinematographer, Teamsters leader\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Nicholson, born John Joseph Nicholson on April 22, 1937, is an American actor and filmmaker who has performed for over 60 years.\n- László Kovács became most famous for his award-winning cinematography on Easy Rider in 1969 and Five Easy Pieces in 1970.\n- Five Easy Pieces stars Jack Nicholson and features Karen Black, Susan Anspach, Ralph Waite, and Sally Struthers in supporting roles.\n- Hoffa is a 1992 French-American biographical crime film directed by Danny DeVito and written by David Mamet.\n- Hoffa is based on the life of Jimmy Hoffa, who was a Teamsters leader.\n- In Hoffa, Jack Nicholson plays Jimmy Hoffa, and Danny DeVito plays Robert Ciaro, a composite character based on several Hoffa associates.\n- László Kovács received numerous awards, including three Lifetime Achievement Awards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
